  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-11-27T22:23:22.049Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Animators are still broken for some AV2 avatars, and I've especially noticed this with ones that toggle gameobjects - for example, you used to be able to have one or more gestures that'd enable a trail/light/etc, and then another set of gestures that'd disable them, with whatever object you were toggling being off by default. Now every animation clip seems to play/initialize simoultaneously upon avatar load, which completely breaks the animator's intended functionality (starts with trails/lights on by default with no way to turn them off, etc)\n\nThis started happening in build 1004, and has continued right through the most recent beta that closed on the 25th. Hoping this gets fixed soon c:\nThis issue seems to be related to these other posts:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1019-av2-inventory-systems-broken (Marked as Complete, though I personally didn't see any difference)\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1004-some-animations-are-playing-repeatedly (Seems to be the same/a very similar issue, with more focus on SDK3 avatars)\n\n12/3/2020 edit: Can confirm that this is still happening in today's release, gesture-toggled things are still broken",
